                     /fragment="True"
                     /other="CDS"
                     /description="Protein evidence at protein level: Swiss-Prot
                     protein existence level 1. Mediates transposition of
                     transposon Tn5 by a 'cut and paste' mechanism. First, the
                     monomeric transposase binds the 19 bp inverted DNA repeats
                     flanking the transposon. Then, dimerization of the
                     DNA-bound transposase creates a synaptic DNA complex. After
                     nicking of the first DNA strand, excision of the transposon
                     proceeds through a series of intermediates. The transposase
                     then mediates the insertion of the transposon at a new site
                     by strand transfer. The activity of the wild-type
                     transposase is very low, and is further inhibited by
                     dimerization with the transposase inhibitor (inh). From
                     Escherichia coli."
